<!--
  RUT_CrackedLandsItems.xml              UtinniPatches · COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1

  Crack-wax, the_cracked_lands.md §11 "Uniquely available": "Crack-wax — the
  Sealed's shed burrow lining, gathered off the flats after a wake; the
  waterproofing the Farmers line their cisterns with. The biome's signature
  material." Companion item to RUT_SealedSleeper.xml (same commission,
  ledger:the_cracked_lands:sealed-signature-sleeper-wax-lined-burrow-
  water-wake-sheds-c).

  Waterproofing/adhesive material, same ResourceBase shape RUT_Bitumen.xml
  (this mod, the_sump kit) already used for an analogous "biome's signature
  substance" resource.

  NOT BUILT THIS PASS, honestly, same posture RUT_Bitumen's own header
  used: the real "gathered off the flats after a wake" harvest job (a
  field-sweep after a Sealed individual wakes and abandons its burrow) is
  not stock and is not authored here — RUT_SealedSleeper.xml's own header
  explains why and files the dedicated item for it
  (`CRACKED_LANDS_SEALED_WAKE_MECHANISM_1`). This ThingDef is real and
  immediately usable (tradeable/debug-spawnable, and wired as a
  butcherProducts yield on the Sealed as an interim source) but has no
  gather job yet.

  Texture: placeholder only, same class as RUT_Bitumen/RUT_ThrummelSeepwax
  (UtinniPatches already claims Textures/Things/Item/Resource/ as its own
  namespace, so a borrowed vanilla icon would hard-error validate_patch.py)
  — repointed to a new RUT_CrackWax/ folder, expected pending texPath.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RUT_CrackWax</defName>
    <label>crack-wax</label>
    <description>A pale, waxy lining shed by a Sealed sleeper when it finally wakes and abandons its burrow. Farmers gather it off the flats and line their cisterns with it — the one waterproofing material the Cracked Lands make for free, and the surest sign a dowsing walk found real water.</description>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RUT_CrackWax</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
      <color>(222, 210, 176)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>60</MaxHitPoints>
      <MarketValue>2.2</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.3</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.4</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>0.5</DeteriorationRate>
    </statBases>
    <stackLimit>100</stackLimit>
    <techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
